WEBVTT

00:02.310 --> 00:04.610
-The Mourner's Eyes-

00:04.610 --> 00:08.030
Episode 2

00:10.150 --> 00:11.860
When will this child be seen?
On this day, in high autumn, he was born.

00:11.860 --> 00:13.700
Zihang, Zihang,

00:13.700 --> 00:15.410
Chu Zihang,

00:15.410 --> 00:16.850
welcome to the family.

00:16.850 --> 00:17.950
Come on, smile!

00:21.950 --> 00:23.870
Since the city first spoke his name,
he has shared this old man's renown.

00:21.950 --> 00:23.870
Poetry is our family's art,
passed down with worldly acclaim.

00:24.450 --> 00:25.540
Kite.

00:25.540 --> 00:26.450
Kite!

00:26.450 --> 00:28.920
Kites are never far away
from the person flying them,

00:28.920 --> 00:31.040
because they are connected
by the kite string.

00:31.040 --> 00:33.040
It's just like our family.

00:33.040 --> 00:34.300
I'll help.

00:38.260 --> 00:39.930
Master the depths of <i>Literary Selections</i>,
leave silken robes unturned.

00:38.260 --> 00:39.930
At his frail feast, the first toast
wavers, his seat tilting, unsteady.

00:41.410 --> 00:42.830
Zihang, this way!

00:42.830 --> 00:43.770
Dad is here to get you.

00:43.770 --> 00:45.250
Get in the car.

00:45.250 --> 00:47.150
Such heavy rain. Hurry.

00:50.790 --> 00:52.070
Let's go.

00:56.870 --> 00:59.370
You and Mom have been arguing a lot lately.

01:01.060 --> 01:02.050
Yes...

01:03.000 --> 01:05.920
I might have to leave for a while.

01:06.870 --> 01:07.830
For how long?

01:09.870 --> 01:13.300
This might be the last time I pick you up.

01:15.190 --> 01:18.800
Don't worry. You're more
important than anything else.

01:19.050 --> 01:20.250
While I'm not around,

01:20.250 --> 01:22.620
remember to give your mom a
cup of warm milk every night,

01:22.620 --> 01:24.350
and add a half spoonful of sugar...

01:24.350 --> 01:25.980
...so Mom can sleep well.

01:26.430 --> 01:27.550
That's right!

01:28.190 --> 01:29.980
Like scattered subset clouds, sip by sip, the wine spills slow and steady.
The poet marks his son's birth, noting that it happened in mid-autumn, a time of maturity and harvest - perhaps symbolizing hope for the child's future.
The son is now known because of his father's literary reputation. The family has a tradition of literary excellence, and the father takes pride in this heritage.
The Wen Xuan was a classic anthology in Chinese literature.
The father urges the son to study it deeply rather than seeking shallow praise
The poet, likely ill or aging, struggles to sit upright during the birthday celebration. He drinks slowly, savoring the moment, but the imagery hints at life's fleeting nature.

01:40.450 --> 01:41.990
Divorce Certificate

01:45.450 --> 01:48.750
Yes, Mom and Dad are getting divorced,

01:48.750 --> 01:50.790
because Dad has no money.

01:50.790 --> 01:52.000
But it's fine.

01:52.000 --> 01:54.000
I'm going to make lots of money soon,

01:54.000 --> 01:55.870
and then remarry your mom.

01:55.870 --> 01:57.380
Soon, very soon.

02:00.140 --> 02:02.610
Zihang, this is your new dad.

02:02.610 --> 02:03.890
Hello, Zihang.

02:03.890 --> 02:04.640
Father

02:05.560 --> 02:07.870
She got remarried so quickly,

02:07.870 --> 02:10.190
and found such a rich and handsome guy.

02:11.310 --> 02:15.190
But it's fine, Zihang.
You'll inherit a fortune in the future.

02:15.190 --> 02:16.820
It's not so bad,
having two dads who love you.

02:25.250 --> 02:27.250
Typhoon emergency alert.

02:27.830 --> 02:30.540
This year's typhoon number 0407, "Dandelion,"

02:30.540 --> 02:33.590
will make landfall on the east coast
of our city this afternoon.

02:33.590 --> 02:34.710
Hey...

02:35.460 --> 02:39.540
I-I'm Lu Mingfei. The weather
bureau said a typhoon's coming.

02:39.540 --> 02:41.090
You should go home early.

02:42.750 --> 02:43.910
I'm leaving now.

02:48.080 --> 02:49.090
A typhoon...

02:51.880 --> 02:52.500
Mom.

02:52.500 --> 02:53.060
Zihang.

02:53.790 --> 02:55.800
I'm shopping with my sisters.

02:55.800 --> 02:57.160
It's raining heavily,

02:57.160 --> 02:58.880
so call a cab and hurry home,

02:58.880 --> 03:01.690
or call your dad and
have him send a car, dear.

03:05.770 --> 03:07.610
I just wanted to tell you that I'm fine.

03:08.250 --> 03:09.500
Go ahead and have fun.

03:11.120 --> 03:12.120
Heavy, heavy rain...

03:12.120 --> 03:14.000
Let's get home quickly!

03:20.800 --> 03:22.830
I should get someone to pick me up.

03:29.230 --> 03:30.100
Dad
Okay.

03:29.230 --> 03:30.100
Dad (New)
[emoji]

03:33.160 --> 03:34.620
Can you come pick me up?

03:34.620 --> 03:37.070
Wait at the school. I'll be there soon!

03:39.330 --> 03:41.030
Can't let new dad see this.

03:48.540 --> 03:50.000
Son!

03:50.000 --> 03:51.460
Long time no see!

03:51.460 --> 03:54.580
Get in! You'll get soaked.
Come on, quickly!

04:09.210 --> 04:10.290
Did your clothes get wet?

04:10.290 --> 04:12.020
I turned on the heated seats for you.

04:12.850 --> 04:13.950
This car is amazing.

04:13.950 --> 04:15.060
It cost nine million yuan.

04:15.060 --> 04:16.400
Our boss just bought it.

04:16.400 --> 04:17.900
It can drive by itself.

04:17.900 --> 04:18.900
Let's go.

04:18.900 --> 04:20.500
Let me show you something cool.

04:22.030 --> 04:24.450
Start!

04:24.450 --> 04:25.650
Voice confirmed.

04:25.650 --> 04:26.250
Starting.

04:27.870 --> 04:30.790
A nine-million-yuan car with voice control.

04:30.790 --> 04:32.640
Just shout and the car goes.

04:32.640 --> 04:35.040
There are only three people
in the world who can start it.

04:35.040 --> 04:36.950
One is me, another is the boss...

04:36.950 --> 04:38.500
Guess who the third one is.

04:39.710 --> 04:42.170
It's you, silly boy.

04:52.680 --> 04:54.640
Damn this traffic jam.

04:54.640 --> 04:57.370
I can't unleash this
nine-million-yuan car at all.

05:08.840 --> 05:10.200
Are you all stupid?

05:10.200 --> 05:12.290
Isn't there a small road
that leads to the overpass?

05:12.780 --> 05:15.000
Oh, I'm not sure if the overpass is closed.

05:15.000 --> 05:16.080
Let's check it out.

05:16.080 --> 05:17.050
Better than being stuck here.

05:20.100 --> 05:22.060
Not a car on this small road!

05:23.420 --> 05:25.330
Look, we can go up!

05:26.870 --> 05:28.660
What if it's closed and we can't get down?

05:28.660 --> 05:30.540
If you can go up, then you can get down.

05:30.540 --> 05:32.170
It's just a matter of passing a cigarette.

05:43.420 --> 05:44.870
Such good luck!

05:44.870 --> 05:46.040
Let's have some music.

05:46.790 --> 05:47.740
Music!

05:52.700 --> 05:53.700
Not bad!

05:53.700 --> 05:55.930
I bought it because they
said it was a good CD.

05:55.930 --> 05:57.660
It's about fatherly love.

05:58.140 --> 06:01.040
This song is written by a father
for a daughter, not a son.

06:01.580 --> 06:02.880
It's not appropriate for
you to play it to me.

06:03.580 --> 06:04.780
You understand it?

06:04.780 --> 06:08.300
That's right. I heard you won a
prize in an English competition.

06:08.300 --> 06:09.340
What's this song about?

06:09.840 --> 06:11.240
It's about a father

06:11.240 --> 06:15.060
who married off his 24-year-old daughter
to a 14-year-old rich boy against her will

06:15.060 --> 06:17.680
so that she would have someone
to rely on in her old age.

06:17.680 --> 06:20.270
In the end, the boy died before he grew up.

06:21.250 --> 06:23.040
Wh-What the hell?

06:23.040 --> 06:24.940
That's no fun. Turn it off.

06:24.940 --> 06:27.230
Let's just chat.

06:27.230 --> 06:30.320
Oh, did I tell you about the
new building our company built?

06:30.320 --> 06:31.410
You talk too much.

06:32.450 --> 06:34.200
By relying on your mouth,

06:34.200 --> 06:36.540
you've been leading on Mom from the start.

06:36.540 --> 06:38.030
You've been a driver for life.

06:38.540 --> 06:40.450
After deducting your monthly expenses,

06:40.450 --> 06:41.770
you can't even afford to raise a cat.

06:42.250 --> 06:44.450
Why did I ask you to pick me up?

06:44.450 --> 06:47.590
Because when you pick me up, we can talk.

06:47.900 --> 06:50.010
Why not just ask how I've been getting on?

06:50.660 --> 06:51.940
Don't hold an umbrella for me.

06:51.940 --> 06:53.180
You're so attentive.

06:53.180 --> 06:54.470
I don't care about that.

06:54.470 --> 06:55.930
I don't need a driver.

06:57.000 --> 06:58.130
What a loser.

06:59.950 --> 07:00.750
So...

07:01.280 --> 07:02.880
How's your mom been lately?

07:02.880 --> 07:04.370
Is she getting a nightly
cup of warm milk

07:04.370 --> 07:05.500
with a half spoonful of sugar?

07:05.500 --> 07:06.560
What about your stepdad?

07:06.560 --> 07:08.700
You need to keep an eye on him,

07:08.700 --> 07:10.160
and don't let him have an affair,

07:10.160 --> 07:12.160
or someone will fight you for your inheritance.

07:12.870 --> 07:15.750
In my opinion, you should
go to university in the country,

07:15.750 --> 07:18.000
and get your stepdad to
sort out your connections.

07:18.580 --> 07:20.950
Since your stepdad is
rich and well-connected,

07:20.950 --> 07:23.330
he can pave the way for your future...

07:23.680 --> 07:25.120
Shut up.

07:25.120 --> 07:26.840
So many people will envy you!

07:28.210 --> 07:29.170
Shut up.

07:29.870 --> 07:30.630
What did you say?

07:30.630 --> 07:32.030
Shut up!

07:36.450 --> 07:39.500
I'm saying this for your own good.

07:39.500 --> 07:41.310
You should listen to adults more.

07:41.310 --> 07:43.270
How useful is it to listen to you?

07:43.270 --> 07:44.410
If I listen to you,

07:44.410 --> 07:46.480
can I find a girl to marry
and not get divorced?

07:46.480 --> 07:47.660
If I listen to you,

07:47.660 --> 07:49.820
then I'll just ask my stepdad
to sort out my connections!

07:56.560 --> 07:58.510
You're still young.

07:58.510 --> 07:59.950
About family matters...

08:00.240 --> 08:01.370
Stay out of my business.

08:01.720 --> 08:03.500
How can you say that?

08:03.500 --> 08:05.460
I'm your real dad.

08:05.460 --> 08:06.670
Real dad...

08:07.500 --> 08:09.750
If you were my real dad,

08:09.750 --> 08:11.500
you would've been at
my parent-teacher conference.

08:11.500 --> 08:14.030
D-Didn't the boss have
a b-big client that day?

08:14.030 --> 08:15.340
Do you remember my birthday?

08:15.340 --> 08:17.160
How could I forget your birthday?

08:17.160 --> 08:18.660
You're my son.

08:18.660 --> 08:21.830
Your mom and I gave birth to you.

08:21.830 --> 08:23.980
Men also contribute to having children.

08:23.980 --> 08:25.750
Have you ever worked hard after having me?

08:25.750 --> 08:27.150
Have you ever taken care of me?

08:27.150 --> 08:29.520
Tell me what it means to be a real father.

08:29.520 --> 08:31.830
A real father means...

08:31.830 --> 08:32.660
that...

08:33.410 --> 08:34.940
my blood flows within you.

08:39.280 --> 08:42.540
I know I haven't been there
for you the last few years.

08:42.540 --> 08:46.880
I'm sorry, but there is no father
who doesn't care about his children.

08:46.880 --> 08:48.670
We're connected by blood.

08:49.850 --> 08:51.550
Let's just co-exist and get along.

08:51.920 --> 08:55.940
Having a child is like giving
half of yourself to the child.

08:56.550 --> 08:59.540
After all, everyone will die.

09:00.040 --> 09:02.600
When I die, everyone will forget me,

09:02.600 --> 09:04.180
but you'll still be here.

09:04.910 --> 09:06.720
Half of you is me.

09:07.960 --> 09:11.540
It'll be like I left something
behind in this world.

09:11.540 --> 09:14.070
You know how to have children,
but not how to raise them.

09:14.410 --> 09:15.100
I...

09:17.450 --> 09:18.990
I wanted to raise you...

09:23.750 --> 09:24.410
Sit back!

09:39.800 --> 09:40.600
Fasten your seat belt!

09:41.040 --> 09:41.600
What...

09:41.930 --> 09:43.220
What is that?

09:44.490 --> 09:45.340
Hold on.

09:49.860 --> 09:51.740
What's happening?

09:59.410 --> 10:01.020
Don't be scared, son.

10:01.500 --> 10:03.120
That is Spirit Sight.

10:03.120 --> 10:05.110
Your bloodline is being activated.

10:07.410 --> 10:08.620
Spirit Sight?

10:11.910 --> 10:14.880
I don't know if it's your luck, or...

10:19.410 --> 10:23.640
I always hoped that this day...
would come later.

10:23.640 --> 10:24.830
What's going on?

10:25.270 --> 10:28.190
Are we going to die?

10:28.190 --> 10:29.740
It's fine, son.

10:30.320 --> 10:31.860
Welcome to...

10:32.250 --> 10:34.110
the real world.

10:34.110 --> 10:36.280
The real world?

10:36.280 --> 10:39.990
Actually, I felt happier
living in a fake world,

10:40.380 --> 10:43.280
so I figured you'd be better off
finding out about this later.

10:43.980 --> 10:47.540
I always thought that if I stayed away
from you, then you wouldn't get involved.

10:49.630 --> 10:51.200
Oh, well.

10:51.200 --> 10:55.750
It seems like someone has
set the stage for us!

11:10.200 --> 11:11.980
Divine Blade Murasame.

11:11.980 --> 11:13.520
The original was destroyed long ago.

11:13.520 --> 11:15.760
They reforged it with recycled metal.

11:15.760 --> 11:18.570
It's a demon sword that has been enshrined
in the Gion Shrine for ten years.

11:24.320 --> 11:25.100
Is it dead?

11:25.100 --> 11:26.280
Don't worry.

11:26.280 --> 11:28.580
The Nibelungen Death Servitors
don't have citizenship.

11:28.580 --> 11:31.540
They're not human, so the
law won't protect them.

11:50.100 --> 11:51.560
This car's not bad.

12:06.670 --> 12:07.580
Call the police.

12:07.930 --> 12:08.820
It's useless.

12:08.820 --> 12:11.700
This is the legendary country
of the dead, Nibelungen.

12:11.700 --> 12:13.940
Everything is made up of dead elements,

12:13.940 --> 12:16.290
Even the city itself is built
from the bones of the dead.

12:16.290 --> 12:17.590
There's no way your phone will work.

12:17.590 --> 12:19.580
Nibelungen? Death Servitors?

12:19.580 --> 12:21.200
It's too much to explain right now.

12:21.200 --> 12:23.170
Just think of Nibelungen as another world,

12:23.170 --> 12:25.980
and Death Servitors are undead
resulting from hybrids transforming.

12:25.980 --> 12:26.850
Hybrids?

12:26.850 --> 12:27.940
Fasten your seat belt.

12:27.940 --> 12:29.470
This car can drive itself.

12:29.470 --> 12:32.640
I'm going to take care of them!

13:01.210 --> 13:02.140
Hold on!

13:02.140 --> 13:02.960
Let's go!

13:12.870 --> 13:13.930
All sorted!

13:14.250 --> 13:15.380
Are you okay, son?

13:16.020 --> 13:16.980
What on earth...

13:16.980 --> 13:18.290
Don't be scared, son.

13:18.290 --> 13:20.900
Once a dad, always a dad.

13:20.900 --> 13:23.380
I'm still your dad, not a monster.

13:24.160 --> 13:27.160
You have also inherited my bloodline,

13:27.160 --> 13:28.450
which is different from others.

13:28.450 --> 13:30.620
If you don't want your stepdad
to sort out your connections,

13:30.620 --> 13:32.730
you can go abroad, since you're
good at foreign languages.

13:32.730 --> 13:35.540
But make sure you don't
go to Cassel College.

13:35.540 --> 13:37.580
The people there are crazy.

13:37.580 --> 13:40.130
I'm telling you, you need to
keep an eye on your stepdad.

13:40.130 --> 13:41.370
Where are we going now?

13:43.910 --> 13:44.970
A toll booth?

13:46.450 --> 13:48.290
We should be back in the normal area.

13:48.290 --> 13:49.700
You can get off after the toll booth.

13:49.700 --> 13:52.310
See if there's anyone
passing by and get a ride.

13:52.310 --> 13:54.350
Then... where are you going?

13:54.870 --> 13:56.560
They'll be coming after me,

13:56.560 --> 13:58.980
because there's something
in the car that they want.

13:58.980 --> 14:00.580
But it'll be fine.

14:00.580 --> 14:02.690
Didn't you see how awesome I was just now?

14:06.540 --> 14:08.110
Don't worry.

14:08.110 --> 14:10.370
I still need to attend the
parent-teacher conference.

14:10.620 --> 14:12.200
Screw the boss!

14:12.200 --> 14:14.450
You're the most important, son.

14:18.220 --> 14:19.460
They...

14:20.700 --> 14:21.620
Horses?

14:22.290 --> 14:23.800
Why can I hear horses?

14:25.870 --> 14:26.970
Hold on to your seat belt!

14:31.370 --> 14:32.880
Damn...

14:33.450 --> 14:34.390
Are you okay, son?

14:40.000 --> 14:42.200
It's your first time seeing
something like that.

14:42.200 --> 14:44.300
Your worldview is bound to collapse.

14:45.330 --> 14:46.940
But now that you've seen it,

14:47.620 --> 14:49.130
open your eyes,

14:49.830 --> 14:51.140
and face it.

15:00.410 --> 15:01.170
That...

15:02.070 --> 15:03.550
is Odin.

15:04.130 --> 15:05.460
A god?

15:05.460 --> 15:06.590
Don't be scared.

15:07.050 --> 15:09.800
Although I was also terrified
when I first saw him,

15:10.750 --> 15:12.680
but fear is useless.

15:13.040 --> 15:13.930
Remember.

15:14.620 --> 15:16.570
You still have me by your side.

15:19.810 --> 15:21.690
Take the briefcase under your feet.

15:22.160 --> 15:23.360
We'll get out together.

15:25.700 --> 15:28.660
Long time no see, big guy.

15:28.660 --> 15:31.820
The throne of god is in front of you.

15:31.820 --> 15:35.610
Humans, present yourselves!

15:35.610 --> 15:37.990
Humans...

15:37.990 --> 15:41.010
We see humans again.

15:41.010 --> 15:41.720
They're speaking.

15:41.720 --> 15:43.250
Don't worry about that.

15:43.250 --> 15:45.000
You've disobeyed me many times before,

15:45.000 --> 15:47.050
but this time, you must do as I say.

15:47.050 --> 15:50.300
Remember, do not leave my side.

15:50.640 --> 15:52.750
I know what you want.

15:52.750 --> 15:53.800
It's right here.

15:53.800 --> 15:57.350
Give me the briefcase.

15:57.350 --> 15:59.890
Remember, when I say "run,"

15:59.890 --> 16:01.440
you run to the car,

16:01.440 --> 16:02.850
and don't look back.

16:06.110 --> 16:08.750
Even if I give it to you,

16:08.750 --> 16:10.860
I doubt you'll let us go.

16:11.100 --> 16:12.150
No.

16:12.750 --> 16:15.500
I promise you your lives.

16:15.500 --> 16:18.870
Gods never lie to mortals.

16:21.080 --> 16:23.380
Then you're not willing to let us go?

16:24.230 --> 16:26.880
Everyone who comes to this country

16:27.320 --> 16:31.090
must become a servant of god.

16:33.590 --> 16:35.510
It seems negotiations have broken down.

16:36.680 --> 16:40.970
Son, remember every word I told you.

16:41.670 --> 16:45.390
Trust me! I'll be at the
parent-teacher conference.

16:47.010 --> 16:48.480
Here you go!

16:48.910 --> 16:50.820
Don't let the briefcase get damaged!

16:53.410 --> 16:54.200
It's empty.

16:54.200 --> 16:55.320
Run!

16:58.570 --> 16:59.410
Get in quickly!

16:59.410 --> 17:00.540
Start the car!

17:00.540 --> 17:01.770
The car can drive itself!

17:01.770 --> 17:02.540
Get in the car!

17:02.540 --> 17:03.470
Do as I say!

17:03.470 --> 17:04.790
Remember what you promised me!

17:04.790 --> 17:05.460
But...

17:05.460 --> 17:08.880
If I die, I still have
you left in this world.

17:08.880 --> 17:10.250
But if you also die,

17:10.250 --> 17:12.620
then I'll have nothing!

17:13.070 --> 17:14.420
If you stay here,

17:14.420 --> 17:16.680
I can't use my ultimate moves.

17:16.680 --> 17:18.120
Trust me.

17:18.120 --> 17:21.730
If you live on, we will see each other again!

17:24.270 --> 17:25.750
Next time it rains,

17:25.750 --> 17:28.860
I'll still come pick you up, son.

17:30.980 --> 17:32.160
Start!

17:43.910 --> 17:45.450
Stop him!

17:45.450 --> 17:46.800
One minute.

17:47.580 --> 17:49.710
Stopping you for one minute

17:49.710 --> 17:53.710
means that nine-million-yuan
car can leave Nibelungen.

17:53.710 --> 17:55.380
Yanling:

17:56.170 --> 17:57.680
Zero Time!

18:01.720 --> 18:04.060
It looks like Zero Time doesn't affect you.

18:04.420 --> 18:07.520
Yanling is the language of the gods.

18:07.520 --> 18:10.060
How would it affect me?

18:10.060 --> 18:11.820
No matter what the enemy is,

18:12.600 --> 18:14.070
I'll cut it open!

18:57.290 --> 18:59.860
Dad!

19:17.930 --> 19:19.050
This is...

19:25.250 --> 19:26.140
Dad.

19:28.410 --> 19:29.280
Dad.

19:31.540 --> 19:32.310
Dad.

19:38.370 --> 19:39.550
Dad!

19:43.250 --> 19:46.050
Dad!

19:57.090 --> 20:00.590
Overpass closed.
Cleanup in progress.

19:57.450 --> 19:58.870
I'll check out that side.

20:00.200 --> 20:01.590
Everyone, nice and steady.

20:02.560 --> 20:03.900
Who can help over here?

20:04.320 --> 20:05.200
I'm coming.

20:05.200 --> 20:06.210
Be careful.

20:10.330 --> 20:11.380
Help.

20:12.000 --> 20:13.870
Everyone, nice and steady.

20:13.870 --> 20:15.050
Help.

20:16.050 --> 20:17.900
Is this the last car?

20:18.480 --> 20:20.690
Yes, this is the last car.

20:23.750 --> 20:24.710
He's gone.

20:25.700 --> 20:26.450
Dad...

20:28.410 --> 20:29.420
is gone.

20:38.750 --> 20:39.710
Brother,

20:40.450 --> 20:41.870
aren't you flying to Xinguo tonight?

20:41.870 --> 20:42.920
Why are you still here?

20:43.660 --> 20:44.670
I noticed the rain,

20:45.380 --> 20:46.840
and a song came to mind.

20:46.840 --> 20:49.260
A song? What song? Is it nice?

20:50.250 --> 20:51.180
Let's listen together.

20:55.190 --> 20:56.480
An English song?

20:56.480 --> 20:58.190
What are the lyrics about?

21:00.540 --> 21:01.550
The lyrics...

21:02.950 --> 21:04.650
are very close to one of my memories.

21:07.450 --> 21:09.250
It's written by a father for a daughter...

21:12.500 --> 21:13.500
Dad,

21:15.000 --> 21:16.340
it's raining again.
